# config.properties, in setup() BEFORE WdCfg.load and CfgPub.start (Skyy 2026-10-15: "id start with 10 loadouts."). Nothing to do = no file
# (seed writes the 0.2.2 default, marker included) or a comment line holding FREE_MIG_ID (done before). Else, per logical line (the kit's own
# parser): slots.free whose LAST entry is a one-line entry holding exactly 4 (the old default) -> every such one-line entry 10 (value text
# only; key, separator, CR kept); NO slots.free entry (it read the code default 4) -> slots.free=10 appended; any other value is an admin's
# choice: KEPT (an INFO line). A change = one config-changes.log line slots.free 4 -> 10 (Server Setup -> Changes -> Undo = 4). The marker
# goes right under the last (or the appended) entry, in the file's own line ending. Properties check (only slots.free differs / is added),
# config-history copy FIRST (verified: it holds exactly the old bytes), the kit's atomicWrite. A failure = WARN, the file untouched, the next
# start tries again. Loadouts are never touched: WdSlots.unlocked reads slots.free live, so every profile simply has 10 open (5-10 empty).
